# Stage A Haxe test runner for the translated core slice, full double precision.
#
# This is tests/compile.hxml with the \`-D float-precision=f32\` line removed.
# The define is the only place the Haxe bundle can leave binary64: the JS
# target has no binary32 representation, but engine-haxe/src/org/tiqian/core/
# AccurateSum.hx branches on \`#if float_precision\` and picks a different
# accumulation shape when the define is present. Layer 3 compares two
# double-precision targets, so the reference bundle must run the f64 branch.
# Output goes to its own file so the f32 bundle stays runnable beside it.
#
#   haxe engine-haxe/tests/compile-js-f64.hxml
#   bun engine-haxe/out/haxe-tests-f64.js
-lib boring
-cp .haxelib/boring/git/samples
-cp engine-haxe/src
-cp engine-haxe/macros
-cp engine-haxe/tests
-main Main
-js engine-haxe/out/haxe-tests-f64.js
-D analyzer-optimize
-D boring_oracle
--macro Intercept.run(['engine-haxe/src'])
--macro GoldenDataMacros.init()
--macro haxe.macro.Compiler.addGlobalMetadata('org.tiqian', '@:build(std.RecordMember.build())')
